{
  "info": {
    "name": "Dhun API",
    "description": "Maintained alongside the code. Any endpoint change — added, removed, renamed, new field, new error code — updates this collection in the SAME change. A stale collection is a broken build.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- Every route lives under `/{{apiVersion}}/` (currently v1). Old app versions stay alive forever, so the prefix is never retrofitted.\n- Auth is `Bearer {{accessToken}}`, set once at collection level and inherited.\n- **Every money endpoint requires an `Idempotency-Key` header** (a UUID). The collection pre-request script generates one automatically for any request whose URL contains `/wallet/`, `/gifts/`, `/cosmetics/` or `/payouts/`.\n- `X-Trace-Id` is echoed back on every response and included in every error body. Quote it in bug reports.\n\n## Error envelope\n\nEvery failure looks like this:\n\n```json\n{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"INSUFFICIENT_BALANCE\", \"message\": \"...\", \"details\": {}, \"trace_id\": \"...\" } }\n```\n\nSwitch on `code`, never on the HTTP status or the message.\n\n## Folder status\n\nFolders map to milestones in `docs/build-plan.md`. Empty ones are not yet built — they are here so the structure is agreed before the endpoints land.\n\n## Errors\n\nEvery failure uses the same envelope. Switch on `code`, never on the status or the message.\n\n```json\n{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"details\": {}, \"trace_id\": \"...\" } }\n```\n\n| Code | Status | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `VALIDATION_FAILED` | 422 | `details.issues[]` carries `field`, `code`, `message`. Field paths only — your input is never echoed back. |\n| `UNSAFE_PAYLOAD` | 400 | Body contained `__proto__` / `constructor` / `prototype` |\n| `BAD_JSON` | 400 | Body was not valid JSON |\n| `UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE` | 415 | Content-Type must be application/json |\n| `PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE` | 413 | Body over 256 KB |\n| `UNAUTHENTICATED` / `INVALID_TOKEN` | 401 | Missing or bad bearer token |\n| `REGISTRATION_REQUIRED` | 403 | Guest tried to spend — verify a phone first |\n| `DOB_REQUIRED` | 403 | **Adult gate.** No date of birth on file. Open the date picker. |\n| `FORBIDDEN` | 403 | Under 18, or missing a role |\n| `RATE_LIMITED` | 429 | Check `Retry-After` and the `RateLimit-*` headers |\n| `IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REQUIRED` / `_INVALID` | 400 | Money endpoints need a UUID key |\n| `IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED` | 422 | Same key, different operation — a client bug |\n| `INSUFFICIENT_BALANCE` | 402 | |\n| `SIGNATURE_INVALID` / `RECEIPT_INVALID` | 402 | Payment did not verify |\n| `RECEIPT_ALREADY_USED` | 409 | Receipt redeemed by another account |\n| `TXN_TYPE_INACTIVE` | 503 | Kill switch is on for that flow |\n| `SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE` / `TIMEOUT` | 503 / 504 | Transient — safe to retry |\n| `INTERNAL_ERROR` | 500 | Always generic. Quote the `trace_id`. |\n\n## Security\n\n- **Unknown fields are rejected, not ignored.** A typo'd key returns 422 rather than being silently dropped.\n- **Rate limits** apply per IP, per device and per user. Guest creation is 5/hour per device; money endpoints 30/min per user.\n- **Money endpoints require a registered adult.** Authenticated, phone-verified, and 18+ with a date of birth on file.\n- 5xx messages are always generic. The detail is in the logs against your `trace_id`.\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequisite",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Money endpoints must carry an Idempotency-Key. Generating it here means",
          "// it is never forgotten by hand, and re-sending the same request in Postman",
          "// exercises a genuine new operation rather than an accidental replay.",
          "const MONEY = ['/wallet/', '/gifts/', '/cosmetics/', '/payouts/'];",
          "const url = pm.request.url.toString();",
          "if (MONEY.some((p) => url.includes(p))) {",
          "  const key = require('uuid').v4();",
          "  pm.environment.set('idempotencyKey', key);",
          "}",
          "",
          "// One trace id per request, echoed back by the server.",
          "pm.environment.set('traceId', require('uuid').v4());"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Applies to every request in the collection.",
          "pm.test('has a trace id', () => {",
          "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Trace-Id')).to.be.a('string');",
          "});",
          "",
          "if (pm.response.code >= 400) {",
          "  pm.test('error uses the standard envelope', () => {",
          "    const body = pm.response.json();",
          "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('error');",
          "    pm.expect(body.error).to.have.property('code');",
          "    pm.expect(body.error).to.have.property('trace_id');",
          "  });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "apiVersion",
      "value": "v1"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "description": "Unversioned on purpose — infrastructure probes should not care about API versions.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Liveness",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Trace-Id",
                "value": "{{traceId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Is the process up? Used by the load balancer. Never touches the database."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('ok', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().ok).to.eql(true));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Readiness",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Trace-Id",
                "value": "{{traceId}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/ready",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "ready"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Can it actually serve? Checks Postgres. Returns 503 when the pool is dead, so a broken instance is pulled from rotation rather than failing user requests."
          },
          "response": [],
